/*
 * snippet::label — the places a diagnostic points at, and what it says there.
 *
 * A `Mark` is a place before it is laid out — the throw site says what it
 * points at, `snippet::layout` decides which excerpt that lands in. A `Span`
 * and a `Label` are the same place after: the byte range of the line to
 * underline, then the run of source under it once the line was cut. A
 * `LabelMsg` is what hangs under the caret, and an `InlineLoc` a place that is
 * cited rather than shown.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::errors::snippet::label
 * @File: ymirc/errors/snippet/label.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
